        "beatId": 8,
        "story": "\"See ya,\" he calls, and holds up his keys in a wave. I'm already walking through the automatic doors, too far gone to wave back. I trot across the asphalt parking lot with slightly heavier than planned shopping bags. The sun has gone down and things are turning shadowy. The creaky squeal of a retirement-aged car trying its darnedest sounds too close behind me. I turn sharply to face a golden sedan that could be considered vintage if the world didn't want to forget this model ever existed. \"You're not walking home with that many groceries, are you?\" Cliff calls from his rolled-down passenger-side window. I shrug as best as I can with the pounds of sugar weighing them down.",
