        "story": "\"Sorry,\" Cliff mutters. \"I don't have too many guests in here. But I think you should know that I realize how bad it is.\" \"It's nice,\" I say. I don't mean it to sound sarcastic. Because even though it's obvious his dog spends many happy a moment in here, the vibe is still good. \"So, what's on your docket now that groceries are sorted?\" he asks. \"See, if you don't want to sound like an undercover HR guy, you're doing a terrible job.\" He chuckles, and we pull out of the lot. \"Okay, now for the obtaining your address part of my covert operation, so I can bug your place and expose your secrets.\" \"Is that an inappropriate joke?\" I lower my lids at him accusingly.",
