        "beatId": 7,
        "story": "I'm heading for the door, danmarki box cradled against my chest -- \"Isn't that Jolene?\" a Persian-accented man calls behind me. I flinch at my name, at who must've said it. Armin's dad calls, \"Jolene!\" The gazes of the other customers crawl to me. I take a breath and turn around. Armin's dad smiles and nods in confirmation. This guy might be a spy if he can recognize me from the low-quality Christmas party picture. I make my way to the table, arms rattling my oversized box of pastries, while Armin's jaw makes its way to the floor. This situation may be the most unprecedented moment in human history; all the words that exist have disappeared from my brain.",
